ion, and authoritarian suppression of dissent during COP29.\n\nPollution remains unchecked at home. Baku and the Absheron Peninsula suffer from decades of oil spills, toxic agrochemicals like DDT, polluted air and water, and rising cancer rates. Environmental laws exist only on paper, while civil society is blocked from meaningful oversight.\n\nReformist voices are punished. Economist and activist Gubad Ibadoghlu warned about the government’s negligence in climate and anti-corruption issues. He was soon arrested on fabricated charges, a signal that even expert dissent is intolerable.\n\nThe bottom line:\n- Azerbaijan’s climate situation is worsening.\n- The government has weakened climate goals and refuses to phase out fossil fuels.\n- Hosting COP29 was a public relations move, not genuine transformation.\n- Pollution and environmental harm continue unchecked.\n\nExperts who speak out are silenced.\n\nIf the state fails to act by strengthening targets, investing in real renewables, ending pollution, and protecting free speech, the climate crisis will deepen. The science is clear. The world is watching. The silence is deadly.\n\n#AzerbaijanClimateCrisis #StopGreenwash #ActNow","entity_set":{"hashtags":[{"indices":[2194,2218],"text":"AzerbaijanClimateCrisis"},{"indices":[2219,2233],"text":"StopGreenwash"},{"indices":[2234,2241],"text":"ActNow"}],"symbols":[],"urls":[],"user_mentions":[]},"richtext":{"richtext_tags":[{"from_index":1652,"to_index":1668,"richtext_types":["Bold"]},{"from_index":1928,"to_index":1963,"richtext_types":["Bold"]}]},"media":{"inline_media":[{"media_id":"1958478869247221760","index":0}]}}}},"grok_analysis_button":true,"community_results":{"result":{"__typename":"Community","id_str":"1953169022381445541","viewer_relationship":{"moderation_state":{"__typename":"CommunityUserDefaultModerationState"}}}},"author_community_relationship":{"community_results":{"result":{"__typename":"Community","id_str":"1953169022381445541","name":"Social Environmental