 policies of the US could well advance this tipping point. Already 2024 was the hottest year on record.\n\nThe world needs tough actions now, not grandstanding slogans for 2050 and beyond.\n\nhttps://t.co/xU47gtf5fg","entity_set":{"hashtags":[],"symbols":[],"urls":[{"display_url":"essd.copernicus.org/articles/17/26…","expanded_url":"https://essd.copernicus.org/articles/17/2641/2025/essd-17-2641-2025.pdf","url":"https://t.co/xU47gtf5fg","indices":[1003,1026]}],"user_mentions":[]}}}},"grok_analysis_button":true,"legacy":{"bookmark_count":26,"bookmarked":false,"created_at":"Sun Jun 22 07:55:38 +0000 2025","conversation_id_str":"1936694554557927849","display_text_range":[0,277],"entities":{"hashtags":[],"symbols":[],"timestamps":[],"urls":[],"user_mentions":[]},"favorite_count":748,"favorited":false,"full_text":"Sixty scientists from reputed institutions from across the world, including two from India, have just published their third annual update of indicators of global climate change. It is a comprehensive analysis. \n\nThere is a faint signal of hope in the update in that the rate of","is_quote_status":false,"lang":"en","quote_count":2,"reply_count":54,"retweet_count":236,"retweeted":false,"user_id_str":"2547533580","id_str":"1936694554557927849"},"id":"1936694554557927849","promoted":false},"id":1141}
