_interstitial_type":"","statuses_count":6170,"translator_type":"none","want_retweets":false,"withheld_in_countries":[]},"location":{"location":""},"media_permissions":{"can_media_tag":true},"parody_commentary_fan_label":"None","profile_image_shape":"Circle","profile_bio":{"description":"The science says 600–1000 ppm of CO₂ plus 1–2°C extra warming hits the sweet spot for all terrestrial and marine life, including human civilization."},"privacy":{"protected":false},"relationship_perspectives":{"following":false},"tipjar_settings":{},"verification":{"verified":false},"profile_description_language":"en"}}},"unmention_data":{},"edit_control":{"initial_tweet_id":"1999723703433564413","edit_control_initial":{"edit_tweet_ids":["1999723703433564413","1999723869033365642"],"editable_until_msecs":"1765609858000","is_edit_eligible":false,"edits_remaining":"4"}},"previous_counts":{"bookmark_count":1,"favorite_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"is_translatable":false,"views":{"count":"20125","state":"EnabledWithCount"},"source":"<a href=\"http://twitter.com/download/android\" rel=\"nofollow\">Twitter for Android</a>","note_tweet":{"is_expandable":true,"note_tweet_results":{"result":{"id":"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE5OTk3MjM4Njg3Mzk3NjQyMjU=","text":"For forty years, we've been sold a single magical number: the 'global average temperature'. This figure has become the barometer for countless policy failures, justified by appeals to climate alarm and dismissive attitudes rooted in historical inequities. Yet this number is deeply flawed—it's not a direct measurement but a constructed estimate. It's wielded as a weapon to push net zero policies, potentially the costliest economic misstep in history, already tallying trillions in spending with no clear end. We have no ironclad proof it's accurate or even meaningful. At best, it's an educated guess, heavily dependent on models and adjustments.\n\nThis elusive metric has helped drive electricity bills skyward across the West, hollow out heavy industries, and shift vast wealth from taxpayers to renewables firms and international organisations. It's also used to marginalise sceptics. And the goalposts keep shifting.\n\nHow is a 'global average temperature' even calculated?\nIt's largely a patchwork of ground stations, many relocated over decades from rural fields to urban airports or tarmac—introducing potential biases like the urban heat island effect. Coverage remains uneven: sparse before 1950, especially over oceans (which cover 70% of Earth) and the Southern Hemisphere. Missing data is 'infilled' via computer algorithms. Raw readings are routinely adjusted—homogenised, infilled, and corrected for urban heat—through complex, often opaque processes.\n\nThe result isn't a true planetary thermometer reading but a modelled reconstruction. Multiple datasets (e.g. from NASA, NOAA, Hadley Centre, Berkeley Earth and Copernicus) exist, each using different methods, and they sometimes diverge on specifics, though they agree on the broad warming trend since the late 19th century.\n\nWe're told to fear catastrophic warming, yet the observed rise is only about +1.2–1.5°C since pre-industrial times (1850–1900 baseline). This may partly reflect natural recovery from the Little Ice Age—a cooler period centred on Eurasia. Over deeper geological time (the Phanerozoic, last 541 million years), Earth's average temperature has often hovered around 19–25°C, far warmer than today's ~15°C, with thriving ecosystems and no human influence. Our current interglacial is relatively cool by those standards; a degree or two of variability fits natural cycles.\n\nSo where's the crisis?\n\nGlobal hurricane frequency shows no clear long-term increase over recent decades (per NOAA and IPCC assessments), though intensity of the strongest storms may be rising. Heatwaves were severe in the 1930s Dust Bowl era (before most CO₂ emissions), with many US records still standing—though today's events are more frequent globally due to better detection and population growth in vulnerable areas. Polar bear populations are stable or higher overall (~26,000 globally) compared to the 1960s, though some subpopulations face sea-ice challenges. The 'crisis' often seems projected 20–30 years ahead—just far enough to sustain current policies (taxes, subsidies) but close enough to maintain urgency.\n\nNext time a headline blares 'Hottest day ever!', remember: it's often from adjusted data fed into models tuned to emphasise warming. Scepticism is branded 'disinformation' to stifle debate. Meanwhile, corporate and globalist interests grow richer as ordinary people foot the bill.\n\nTrue science thrives on questioning constructs like this. A genuine planetary 'average temperature' may be more illusion than reality—and basing trillion-dollar policies on it risks enormous harm for uncertain benefits.","entity_set":{"hashtags":[],"symbols":[],"timestamps":[],"urls":[],"user_mentions":[]},"richtext":{"richtext_tags":[{"from_index":890,"to_index":922,"richtext_types":["Italic"]}]}}}},"grok_analysis_button":true,"legacy":{"bookmark_count":210,"bookmarked":false,"created_at":"Sat Dec 13 06:11:38 +0000 2025","conversation_id_str":"1999723869033365642","display_text_range":[0,274],"entities":{"hashtags":[],"media":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/CTIik390Wl","expanded_url":"https://x.com/PeterDClack/status/1999723869033365642/photo/1","id_str":"1999723699193425920","indices":[275,298],"media_key":"3_1999723699193425920","media_url_https":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/G8ByHANasAAtW7J.jpg","type":"photo","url":"https://t.co/CTIik390Wl","ext_media_availability":{"status":"Available"},"features":{"large":{"faces":[]},"medium":{"faces":[]},"small":{"faces":[]},"orig":{"faces":[]}},"sizes":{"large":{"h":450,"w":800,"resize":"fit"},"medium":{"h":450,"w":800,"resize":"fit"},"small":{"h":383,"w":680,"resize":"fit"},"thumb":{"h":150,"w":150,"resize":"crop"}},"original_info":{"height":450,"width":800,"focus_rects":[{"x":0,"y":2