banners/1688442515412975616/1694764270","profile_interstitial_type":"","statuses_count":6840,"translator_type":"none","url":"https://t.co/7yH7lzurlE","want_retweets":false,"withheld_in_countries":[]},"location":{"location":"India"},"media_permissions":{"can_media_tag":true},"parody_commentary_fan_label":"None","profile_image_shape":"Circle","professional":{"rest_id":"1688443804297384118","professional_type":"Business","category":[{"id":145,"name":"Education Company","icon_name":"IconBriefcaseStroke"}]},"profile_bio":{"description":"Preparing for UPSC? Let's get back to basics as we help set you up for your inevitable glory.   https://t.co/Hzp1txjbUE"},"privacy":{"protected":false},"relationship_perspectives":{"following":false},"tipjar_settings":{},"verification":{"verified":false},"profile_description_language":"en"}}},"unmention_data":{},"edit_control":{"edit_tweet_ids":["1996133235206897889"],"editable_until_msecs":"1764753824000","is_edit_eligible":true,"edits_remaining":"5"},"is_translatable":false,"views":{"count":"4513","state":"EnabledWithCount"},"source":"<a href=\"http://twitter.com/#!/download/ipad\" rel=\"nofollow\">Twitter for iPad</a>","note_tweet":{"is_expandable":true,"note_tweet_results":{"result":{"id":"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE5OTYxMzMyMzUwMjY1MzQ0MDA=","text":"▫️Major Grasslands of the World - Prelims Revision Post\n\nGrasslands cover nearly 25% of Earth’s land surface. \nThey differ by climate, continent, and the communities that adapted to them.\n\nHere’s a quick breakdown:\n\n⸻\n\n1. Prairies – North America\n\nLocation: USA (Great Plains), Canada\nFeatures:\n•Tall grasses in the east, short grasses in the west\n•Richest agricultural lands globally\nCommunities & Occupation:\n•Cowboys; large-scale mechanized wheat farming, cattle ranching.\n\n⸻\n\n2. Pampas – South America\n\nLocation: Argentina, Uruguay, southern Brazil\nFeatures:\n•Temperate grasslands with feathery pampa grass\n•Known for fertile humus-rich soils\nCommunities & Occupation:\n•Gauchos; commercial beef production, cereal farming.\n\n⸻\n\n3. Steppes – Europe & Central Asia\n\nLocation: Ukraine, Russia, Mongolia, Kazakhstan\nFeatures:\n•Short grasses, cold deserts, continental climate\n•Prone to dust storms\nCommunities & Occupation:\n•Nomadic herders; sheep, goat, yak herding, limited farming.\n\n⸻\n\n4. Savannah – Africa, South America, Australia, India\n\nLocation: Largest in Africa (Kenya, Tanzania, Sudan)\nFeatures:\n•Tall coarse grasses, scattered trees\n•Distinct wet & dry seasons\nCommunities & Occupation:\n•Maasai & other tribes; pastoralism, wildlife tourism.\n\n⸻\n\n5. Veld – South Africa\n\nLocation: High plateau of South Africa\nFeatures:\n•Red oat grass dominant\n•Mild climate, scattered shrubs\nCommunities & Occupation:\n•Boers; dairy farming, wool production, mining nearby.\n\n⸻\n\n6. Downs – Australia\n\nLocation: Southeast Australia\nFeatures:\n•Mainly Mitchell grass\n•Open, rolling grass-covered plains\nCommunities & Occupation:\n•Sheep farmers; merino wool industry hub.\n\n⸻\n\nWhy Grasslands Matter?\n\n•Act as major carbon sinks.\n•Home to iconic species (bison, antelope, kangaroos).\n•World’s most productive agro-economic zones.\n•Important in climate and monsoon studies.","entity_set":{"hashtags":[],"symbols":[],"timestamps":[],"urls":[],"user_mentions":[]}}}},"grok_analysis_button":true,"legacy":{"bookmark_count":88,"bookmarked":false,"created_at":"Wed Dec 03 08:23:44 +0000 2025","conversation_id_str":"1996133235206897889","display_text_range":[0,277],"entities":{"hashtags":[],"media":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/P0irOavLbQ","expanded_url":"https://x.com/ProxyGyan/status/1996133235206897889/photo/1","id_str":"1996133227619385346","indices":[278,301],"media_key":"3_1996133227619385346","media_url_https":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/G7OwmDSbgAIAqxO.jpg","type":"photo","url":"https://t.co/P0irOavLbQ","ext_media_availability":{"status":"Available"},"features":{"large":{"faces":[{"x":198,"y":370,"h":133,"w":133}]},"medium":{"faces":